  "id": "COMPOUND:22706 - PROTEIN:5864",
  "verbalization": "Lupinifolin is implicated in the biological activity of U373 MG through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Lupinifolin acts as a target for Phosphatidylinositol 4-kinase type 2-beta, which in turn is targeted by SB-269970 and Myricetin-3-O-Beta-D-Glucuronide. These compounds are all known to interact with U373 MG, indicating a potential role in modulating cellular processes that influence the growth and survival of this cancer cell line. Additionally, Lupinifolin is also linked to the ATP-sensitive potassium channel, which is targeted by 4,4'-Dihydroxybenzophenone, both of which also show a target relationship with U373 MG. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Lupinifolin may exert its effects on U373 MG, potentially through the modulation of intracellular signaling and ion homeostasis. The evidence supports a network of interactions that could contribute to the observed effects on U373 MG, though the exact nature of the molecular interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
